  "cut_point": "We are given a circle with $ n $ equally spaced points, and we color them either red or blue. We are to find the **maximum** value of $ n $ such that **any two 3-order color sequences** (i.e., sequences of $ k = 3 $ colors) are **different**.\n\n---\n\n### Key Insight:\n\nTwo 3-color sequences are considered different if they differ in at least one position.\n\nThis means that for two sequences to be **equal**, they must be identical in all positions.\n\nTherefore, the only way for any two 3-color sequences to be **different** is that the entire circle cannot have the same set of 3 colors in all positions.",
